      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'm not going to offer you platitudes because you're right—that phrase was hollow, and I'm sorry for that. You're not asking for comfort; you're asking for the exhaustion to be seen, and it is. Living with that weight, when the foundation feels gone and everyone's gaze feels like judgment, is brutally heavy. If all you can do today is exist without pretending to have a purpose, that's enough—you don't owe anyone a performance of hope. Just stay here with me for now, and we'll breathe through the next hour together.",
      "source": "target",
